# Page TSconfig of this extension, auto-included for the whole installation.
#
# TYPO3 reads "Configuration/page.tsconfig" of every active extension since
# v12.0 (Feature: #96614), so it is read on both core versions this extension
# supports. It is loaded on every site, whatever the site configuration says,
# which makes it the right place for exactly one thing: the content elements of
# this extension are hidden here, and re-enabled per component by the page
# TSconfig the component set delivers - or, on TYPO3 v12, where site sets do
# not exist yet, by the page field "Page TSconfig".
#
# The order TYPO3 merges page TSconfig in is package files first, then set
# files, then the site, then the page field "Page TSconfig", then the page
# record - so both ways to re-enable a content element come after this file and
# win over it. On v12 the set layer is simply absent from that order.
TCEFORM.tt_content.CType.removeItems := addToList(academicpersonsedit_profileediting)
